      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I tested this out in a few worlds just now with some videos from YouTube and videos from my Google Cloud storage and I didn't seem to have any glitching/crackling/audio skipping, everything sounded fine.\n\nUsually when I am getting glitching/crackling/audio skipping on a video that's played through the VideoSyncPlayer, it's because it's not encoded right or something, and so I'll have to re-encode it using Handbrake with Web Optimized and Fast Decode checked, and Audio set to AAC Passthru which always fixes the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
